%% OutboxEntry state machine (sender device, :mobile:messaging Outbox; State pattern, CAS transitions).
%% ADRs: ADR-0013 (delivery semantics, ticks), ADR-0016 (fail-closed, no plaintext fallback),
%%       ADR-0012 (engine), ADR-0015 (PathPolicy at 1.2), ADR-0025 (HOP_ACKED / serverOwed custody).
%% Status: Proposed - pending owner approval in docs/architecture/multi-transport/APPROVAL.md. No code before approval.
%% Source of truth: decision brief section 6.1 (transition table). Detailed rows T01-T32:
%%   docs/architecture/multi-transport/delivery-engine-spec.md section 4.3 (rows marked "spec" extend the brief).
%% Evidence: MOB-04 (lossy at-most-once outbox), MOB-03, BE-07 (replayed ServerAck), C9 (plaintext fallback), GEM-01/02.
%% Rules:
%%   1. Every transition is a compare-and-set on outbox_entry.state; side effects commit in the same SQLDelight tx.
%%   2. DELIVERED and READ are NOT outbox states; ticks are derived from receipt rows (brief section 6.4).
%%   3. No attempt cap: only lifetime (default 30 d; CONTROL and call signalling 60 s) ends retries.
%%   4. Backoff: full jitter 1 s to 30 s on the injected Clock; reset to now on an eligible LinkUp.
%%   5. Late results from a superseded attempt fail the CAS and are ignored.
%% > **Reviewer note (open):** brief section 6.1 permits RetryDelivery only from FAILED_PERMANENT and lists EXPIRED as
%%   terminal; delivery-engine-spec T26 also allows it from EXPIRED. The EXPIRED --> QUEUED edge is therefore NOT drawn
%%   and is not normative until the owner / brief confirms it.
%% > **Reviewer note (open):** brief section 6.1 says "any non-terminal -> EXPIRED on lifetime", which would include
%%   SERVER_ACCEPTED; spec T27 excludes SERVER_ACCEPTED and T28 purges it on LifetimeExceeded instead (spec reviewer
%%   note R-2). Drawn per the spec reading below; the brief must state one rule.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    state "PREPARING<br/>media compress + resumable upload (1 MiB ranges)<br/>outside conversation FIFO" as PREPARING
    state "PENDING_SEAL(reason)<br/>E2E, no session / untrusted identity<br/>UI: waiting for secure session" as PENDING_SEAL
    state "QUEUED<br/>UI: clock" as QUEUED
    state "IN_FLIGHT(link, attempt, deadline)<br/>lease_until = deadline" as IN_FLIGHT
    state "RETRY_WAIT(nextAttemptAt)" as RETRY_WAIT
    state "HOP_ACKED(custodian, serverOwed)<br/>peer, own device or mule acked<br/>serverOwed = mode != LOCAL_ONLY" as HOP_ACKED
    state "SERVER_ACCEPTED(seq)<br/>UI: one tick; row gets seq" as SERVER_ACCEPTED
    state "FAILED_PERMANENT(code)<br/>UI: tap to retry" as FAILED_PERMANENT
    state "EXPIRED<br/>UI: not sent" as EXPIRED
    state "CANCELLED<br/>row and entry deleted" as CANCELLED

    [*] --> QUEUED : Send (text), optimistic row + entry in one tx
    [*] --> PENDING_SEAL : Send in E2E conversation (1.0+), row + entry in tx, seal requested outside tx [spec T02]
    [*] --> PREPARING : Send (media)

    PREPARING --> PREPARING : UploadFailed(retryable), backoff
    PREPARING --> QUEUED : UploadDone(blobRef), not E2E
    PREPARING --> PENDING_SEAL : UploadDone(blobRef), E2E
    PREPARING --> FAILED_PERMANENT : UploadFailed(non-retryable) [spec]

    PENDING_SEAL --> PENDING_SEAL : SealFailed(NoSession), trigger prekey fetch, NEVER plaintext
    PENDING_SEAL --> QUEUED : SessionReady, then SealOk (sealed once)
    PENDING_SEAL --> QUEUED : IdentityApproved (UNTRUSTED_IDENTITY), re-seal, SealOk [spec T11]
    PENDING_SEAL --> FAILED_PERMANENT : SealFailed(non-retryable) [spec]
    QUEUED --> PENDING_SEAL : SealFailed(NoSession) on re-seal

    QUEUED --> IN_FLIGHT : Dispatch(link), due + link Ready/UP + lane capacity
    RETRY_WAIT --> IN_FLIGHT : Dispatch(link), now >= nextAttemptAt [spec T15]
    RETRY_WAIT --> RETRY_WAIT : EligibleLinkUp, backoff reset to now

    IN_FLIGHT --> SERVER_ACCEPTED : ServerAccepted(seq, ts, replay), replay is not an error
    IN_FLIGHT --> HOP_ACKED : HopAcked(peer / own device / mule)
    IN_FLIGHT --> RETRY_WAIT : Timeout, LinkLost, Retry(after)
    IN_FLIGHT --> RETRY_WAIT : Backpressure(after), attempt not incremented [spec T23]
    IN_FLIGHT --> FAILED_PERMANENT : Rejected(code), permanent code
    IN_FLIGHT --> QUEUED : Recover at process start (server is idempotent)

    HOP_ACKED --> QUEUED : ServerLinkUp and serverOwed, server-only upload, recipient dedups
    HOP_ACKED --> SERVER_ACCEPTED : SeqObserved(seq), a custodian already uploaded [spec]
    HOP_ACKED --> [*] : E2EDelivered and not serverOwed (LOCAL_ONLY), purge

    SERVER_ACCEPTED --> [*] : ReceiptsSettled or LifetimeExceeded [T28], purge entry (row and receipts stay)

    FAILED_PERMANENT --> QUEUED : RetryDelivery (user)
    FAILED_PERMANENT --> [*] : user deletes, purge
    EXPIRED --> [*] : user deletes, purge

    QUEUED --> CANCELLED : user deletes
    RETRY_WAIT --> CANCELLED : user deletes
    PENDING_SEAL --> CANCELLED : user deletes
    PREPARING --> CANCELLED : user deletes [spec T29b]
    CANCELLED --> [*]

    PREPARING --> EXPIRED : lifetime exceeded
    PENDING_SEAL --> EXPIRED : lifetime exceeded
    QUEUED --> EXPIRED : lifetime exceeded
    RETRY_WAIT --> EXPIRED : lifetime exceeded
    IN_FLIGHT --> EXPIRED : lifetime exceeded
    HOP_ACKED --> EXPIRED : lifetime exceeded

    note right of HOP_ACKED
        Ticks (ADR-0013), one meaning on every path:
        direct to recipient device = two ticks + "not yet synced"
        once the sealed L2 DELIVERED receipt is stored
        (HopAck alone = clock)
        own device or mule = clock + "handed to (device or contact)"
        There is never a "relayed to mesh" tick.
    end note

    note left of PENDING_SEAL
        ADR-0016 fail-closed: the plaintext fallback (C9)
        is deleted, not flag-gated. A seal failure parks
        the entry; it never downgrades content.
    end note
